Send the frame stats Steam's bitrate control needs.

Nothing in the app reported a frame as displayed, so the 1 Hz flush never had a frame to fold and
ihslib never sent a CFrameStatsListMsg: a Steam Deck's streaming_log.txt shows every Avg* of
SessionStats at 0. Steam's dynamicbitrate then ran without the client's link bandwidth (stat 17,
the "inst" it logs): in steamui.so a 0 there leaves its link estimate unfed, and after a loss the
target sat at about 4 Mbit/s. With stat 17 the link estimate moves to 0.8 x max(inst, 15 Mbit/s).

- A frame the decoder takes is reported displayed, any other dropped (decode corrupt). Without
  this the drain reported every frame dropped late, and the host cut the frame rate to 30.
- Ping (14), server and client bitrate (15, 16), link bandwidth (17) and packet loss (18) go with
  each flush, from the session counters; the bitrates count the video bytes received, and the
  loss counts FEC shards too, as IHS_SessionGetStreamStats does.
- The flush goes out even when no frame was folded.
- Network duration (stat 6) is no longer sent: it subtracted the host's send time from the
  client's receive time, two different clocks, and the host logged "Slow framerate" with network
  at about 60000000 ms.

With 5% loss for 20 s from a Steam Deck, the target went back to about 12 Mbit/s 7 to 10 s after
the loss stopped, on tsl-cli and on a QN90D. Without this patch it stayed at about 4 Mbit/s.

